IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lpatas-costs`

-- Legal Profession Act 2007 (Tas), Part 3.3 -- worked cases for the client's questions.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are
-- HYPOTHETICAL. Dates are `the calendar date` day month year. Calendar used: 2 November 2026 is a Monday, 6 November 2026
-- a Friday.
--
-- Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (CC BY 4.0, State of Tasmania). For the
-- latest information on Tasmanian Government legislation please go to www.legislation.tas.gov.au.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- a client under Part 3.3 of the Legal Profession Act 2007 (Tas)`

§§ `Short names`

`any day` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2000
`INDIVIDUAL` MEANS `an individual, or another client not in the list below`
`LAWYER` MEANS `a law practice or an Australian legal practitioner (s 295(1)(c)(i))`
`GOVERNMENT` MEANS `a Minister, government department or public authority (s 295(1)(c)(viii))`
`BIG COMPANY` MEANS `a public company, large proprietary company, foreign company, a subsidiary of one, or a registered Australian body (s 295(1)(c)(ii))`
`CLAIM` MEANS `any other matter (for example an injury, compensation, insurance or employment claim)`
`MUST DISCLOSE` MEANS `yes: the law practice must give me written costs disclosure (ss 291, 294)`
`UNDER THRESHOLD` MEANS `no: the likely costs are at most the threshold, but if they become likely to exceed it I must be told as soon as practicable (s 295(1)(a), (2))`
`WAIVED` MEANS `no: I waived it in writing after a disclosure in the last 12 months, and a principal decided further disclosure is not warranted (s 295(1)(b))`
`LISTED` MEANS `no: I am a client in the s 295(1)(c) list (a sophisticated client)`
`TENDER` MEANS `no: the costs were agreed through a tender (s 295(1)(d))`
`NOT PAYING` MEANS `no: I will not have to pay the costs (s 295(1)(e))`
`REGS` MEANS `no: the regulations exempt this case (s 295(1)(f))`
`NOT VOID` MEANS `not void under s 311: no contravention of Division 5 on these facts`
`VOID 309` MEANS `void: it charges a share of what I recover (s 309), so the law practice can recover nothing for its services (s 311(5))`
`VOID 308` MEANS `void: its uplift fee breaks s 308, so the uplift fee cannot be recovered (s 311(4))`
`VOID 307` MEANS `void: it breaks the conditional costs agreement rules (s 307), so costs are recoverable only as s 303 allows, capped at the agreement (s 311(2), (3))`
`VOID 306` MEANS `void: it is not properly made (s 306), so costs are recoverable only as s 303 allows, capped at the agreement (s 311(2), (3))`
`MAY SUE` MEANS `Part 3.3 does not stop the law practice suing me on that day`
`NO BILL` MEANS `no: no bill has been given to me (s 313(1))`
`ASSESSING` MEANS `no: my costs assessment application has not been completed (s 323(b))`
`UNDISCLOSED` MEANS `no: I was not told something Division 3 required, and the costs have not been assessed (s 300(2))`
`ITEMISED OUTSTANDING` MEANS `no: I asked for an itemised bill and it has not been given (s 316(5))`
`TOO EARLY` MEANS `no: it is less than 30 days after the bill or itemised bill, and the court must stay the proceedings (ss 313(1), (3), 316(4), (5))`
`IN TIME` MEANS `yes: the application is in time (s 319(5))`
`COURT MAY EXTEND` MEANS `out of time, but it may be dealt with if the Supreme Court decides that is just and fair, having regard to the delay and its reasons (s 319(6))`
`NO EXTENSION` MEANS `no: out of time, and a sophisticated client cannot have the time extended (s 319(6))`
`CONTRACTED OUT` MEANS `no: as a sophisticated client I contracted out of costs assessment (s 338)`
`PRACTICE PAYS` MEANS `the law practice pays the costs of the assessment, unless the assessor orders otherwise (s 331(2))`
`AS ORDERED` MEANS `whoever the costs assessor orders to pay them (s 331(2), (3))`

§§ `ss 283, 284 -- who I am`

#ASSERT `s 284 -- am I a third party payer` `I am the client myself` EQUALS `not a third party payer (s 284(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `s 284 -- am I a third party payer` `I am legally obliged to pay some or all of the client's costs, and I owe that to the law practice` EQUALS `an associated third party payer (s 284(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 284 -- am I a third party payer` `I am legally obliged to pay some or all of the client's costs, but I owe that only to the client or someone else` EQUALS `a non-associated third party payer (s 284(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `s 284 -- am I a third party payer` `I am a law practice that retained the other law practice for the client, and owe nothing else` EQUALS `not a third party payer (s 284(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `s 284 -- am I a third party payer` `I have no legal obligation to pay the client's costs` EQUALS `not a third party payer (s 284(1), (3))`

#ASSERT `s 283 -- am I a sophisticated client` `INDIVIDUAL` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 283 -- am I a sophisticated client` `INDIVIDUAL` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 283 -- am I a sophisticated client` `LAWYER` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 283 -- am I a sophisticated client` `GOVERNMENT` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 283 -- am I a sophisticated client` `BIG COMPANY` FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§§ `ss 285 to 287 -- does the Part apply`

#ASSERT `s 286(4) -- by what day must I notify` (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 3 2026

-- First instructions in Tasmania (s 285).
#ASSERT `ss 285 to 287 -- does Part 3.3 apply to my matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- ... displaced by choosing another jurisdiction's law for a matter belonging there (s 287(2)).
#ASSERT `ss 285 to 287 -- does Part 3.3 apply to my matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` `any day` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- ... a matter belonging elsewhere, but no choice made: still applies.
#ASSERT `ss 285 to 287 -- does Part 3.3 apply to my matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` `any day` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- First instructions elsewhere: work in Tasmania and an accepted offer (s 286).
#ASSERT `ss 285 to 287 -- does Part 3.3 apply to my matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- ... work in Tasmania, no offer and no notice.
#ASSERT `ss 285 to 287 -- does Part 3.3 apply to my matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- ... an accepted offer, but neither work in nor connection with Tasmania.
#ASSERT `ss 285 to 287 -- does Part 3.3 apply to my matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- ... substantial connection, notice on the 28th day after being told of the right, and on the 29th.
#ASSERT `ss 285 to 287 -- does Part 3.3 apply to my matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 29 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `ss 285 to 287 -- does Part 3.3 apply to my matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 30 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- ... a notice when never told of the right: no time limit runs.
#ASSERT `ss 285 to 287 -- does Part 3.3 apply to my matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `any day` (`the calendar date` 30 12 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- ... where the place of first instructions cannot be determined, with work in Tasmania and an offer accepted.
#ASSERT `ss 285 to 287 -- does Part 3.3 apply to my matter` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `any day` `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§§ `s 295 -- must I be given disclosure`

#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 1500 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `INDIVIDUAL` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `UNDER THRESHOLD`
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 1500.01 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `INDIVIDUAL` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `MUST DISCLOSE`
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 1800 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE `INDIVIDUAL` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `UNDER THRESHOLD`
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 2000 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE `INDIVIDUAL` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `UNDER THRESHOLD`
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 2001 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE `INDIVIDUAL` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `MUST DISCLOSE`
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 1400 1000 FALSE FALSE FALSE `INDIVIDUAL` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `UNDER THRESHOLD`
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 5000 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE `INDIVIDUAL` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `WAIVED`
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 5000 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE `INDIVIDUAL` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `MUST DISCLOSE`
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 5000 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE `INDIVIDUAL` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `MUST DISCLOSE`
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 5000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `LAWYER` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `LISTED`
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 5000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `INDIVIDUAL` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `TENDER`
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 5000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `INDIVIDUAL` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT PAYING`
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 5000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `INDIVIDUAL` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `REGS`
-- Two exceptions: the first in the Act's order is reported.
#ASSERT `s 295 -- must the law practice give me costs disclosure` 1000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `GOVERNMENT` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `UNDER THRESHOLD`

§§ `ss 291, 292 -- was I told everything`

#ASSERT `ss 291, 292 -- was I told everything` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `nothing: everything ss 291 and 292 require was disclosed`
-- Not billed at intervals, no interest charged, not litigious: those items are not needed.
#ASSERT `ss 291, 292 -- was I told everything` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `nothing: everything ss 291 and 292 require was disclosed`
#ASSERT `ss 291, 292 -- was I told everything` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the basis on which costs are calculated, and whether a scale applies (s 291(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `ss 291, 292 -- was I told everything` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `an estimate of total costs, or a range and the major variables (s 291(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `ss 291, 292 -- was I told everything` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the billing intervals (s 291(1)(d))`
#ASSERT `ss 291, 292 -- was I told everything` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the interest rate on overdue costs (s 291(1)(e))`
#ASSERT `ss 291, 292 -- was I told everything` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `in a litigious matter, the range of costs I may recover or be ordered to pay, with the s 291(4) statements (s 291(1)(f))`
#ASSERT `ss 291, 292 -- was I told everything` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the dispute avenues and their time limits (s 291(1)(i), (j))`
#ASSERT `ss 291, 292 -- was I told everything` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the name of the lawyer who will mainly do the work, and whether non-lawyers will do some (s 292)`
-- Two items missing: the first in the Act's order.
#ASSERT `ss 291, 292 -- was I told everything` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `my rights to negotiate a costs agreement, get a bill, ask for an itemised bill within 30 days, and be told of changes (s 291(1)(b))`

§§ `ss 296, 297 -- settlement and uplift disclosure`

#ASSERT `s 296 -- must I be told the costs before settling` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 296 -- must I be told the costs before settling` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 296 -- must I be told the costs before settling` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 296 -- must I be told the costs before settling` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 297 -- must I be told about the uplift fee first` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 297 -- must I be told about the uplift fee first` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 297 -- must I be told about the uplift fee first` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `ss 300, 301 -- failure to disclose, reports`

#ASSERT `s 300(1) -- may I hold off paying until the costs are assessed` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 300(1) -- may I hold off paying until the costs are assessed` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 300(1) -- may I hold off paying until the costs are assessed` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 300(1) -- may I hold off paying until the costs are assessed` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 301 -- can I be charged for the report` `a written report on the progress of my matter (s 301(1)(a))` EQUALS `it must be given on reasonable request, and I may be charged a reasonable amount for it (s 301(2))`
#ASSERT `s 301 -- can I be charged for the report` `a written report of the costs incurred to date or since the last bill (s 301(1)(b))` EQUALS `it must be given on reasonable request, free: the law practice must not charge for it (s 301(2))`

§§ `ss 303, 305 -- basis and interest`

#ASSERT `s 303 -- on what basis are my costs recoverable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `under my costs agreement (s 303(a))`
#ASSERT `s 303 -- on what basis are my costs recoverable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `under the applicable scale of costs (s 303(b))`
#ASSERT `s 303 -- on what basis are my costs recoverable` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the fair and reasonable value of the services (s 303(c))`

#ASSERT `s 305(1) -- from what day can interest be charged` (`the calendar date` 15 1 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 14 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 305 -- may the law practice charge me interest` (`the calendar date` 15 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 14 2 2026) TRUE FALSE 8 10 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 305 -- may the law practice charge me interest` (`the calendar date` 15 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 13 2 2026) TRUE FALSE 8 10 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 305 -- may the law practice charge me interest` (`the calendar date` 15 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 13 2 2026) TRUE TRUE 8 10 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 305 -- may the law practice charge me interest` (`the calendar date` 15 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) FALSE TRUE 8 10 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 305 -- may the law practice charge me interest` (`the calendar date` 15 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE 10 10 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 305 -- may the law practice charge me interest` (`the calendar date` 15 1 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE 10.5 10 EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 307 -- conditional (no-win no-fee) agreements`

#ASSERT `s 307(2) -- can my matter be no-win no-fee` `CLAIM` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 307(2) -- can my matter be no-win no-fee` `criminal proceedings` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307(2) -- can my matter be no-win no-fee` `proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth)` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307(2) -- can my matter be no-win no-fee` `proceedings under the Relationships Act 2003` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307(2) -- can my matter be no-win no-fee` `proceedings under the Adoption Act 1988` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307(2) -- can my matter be no-win no-fee` `proceedings under the Children, Young Persons and Their Families Act 1997` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307(2) -- can my matter be no-win no-fee` `proceedings under the Youth Justice Act 1997` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307(2) -- can my matter be no-win no-fee` `a matter the regulations exclude` EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 307 -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 307 -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307 -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307 -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 10 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307 -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307 -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `CLAIM` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A sophisticated client: no signature, statement or cooling-off needed; writing and success terms still are.
#ASSERT `s 307 -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 307 -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `CLAIM` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307 -- does my no-win no-fee agreement meet the requirements` `proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Cooling-off: made Friday 6 November 2026, 5 clear business days end Friday 13 November.
#ASSERT `s 307(3)(e) -- by what day can I cool off` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 13 11 2026
-- Made Monday 2 November: Tuesday to Friday, then Monday 9 November.
#ASSERT `s 307(3)(e) -- by what day can I cool off` (`the calendar date` 2 11 2026) 5 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 9 11 2026
-- One weekday statutory holiday in the period: Monday 16 November.
#ASSERT `s 307(3)(e) -- by what day can I cool off` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 1 EQUALS `the calendar date` 16 11 2026
-- The agreement gives 10 business days: Friday 20 November.
#ASSERT `s 307(3)(e) -- by what day can I cool off` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 10 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 20 11 2026
-- The agreement gives only 3: the Act's 5 are used.
#ASSERT `s 307(3)(e) -- by what day can I cool off` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 3 0 EQUALS `the calendar date` 13 11 2026
-- Made Wednesday 23 December 2026, across the new year. Under the Statutory Holidays Act 2000 (Tas) (not deposited),
-- Christmas Day falls on Friday 25 December, Boxing Day (Saturday 26) is observed on Monday 28 December, and New
-- Year's Day is Friday 1 January 2027: three weekday holidays. Business days: Thursday 24, Tuesday 29, Wednesday 30,
-- Thursday 31 December, Monday 4 January 2027 -- 8 weekdays, 5 business days.
#ASSERT `s 307(3)(e) -- by what day can I cool off` (`the calendar date` 23 12 2026) 5 3 EQUALS `the calendar date` 4 1 2027
-- The same period with the holidays undercounted (only those before the new year): the answer lands on New Year's Day,
-- which is why the count must run to the end of the extended period (fork F4).
#ASSERT `s 307(3)(e) -- by what day can I cool off` (`the calendar date` 23 12 2026) 5 2 EQUALS `the calendar date` 1 1 2027
#ASSERT `s 307(6) -- did I cool off in time` (`the calendar date` 23 12 2026) 5 3 TRUE (`the calendar date` 4 1 2027) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 307(6) -- did I cool off in time` (`the calendar date` 23 12 2026) 5 3 TRUE (`the calendar date` 5 1 2027) EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 307(6) -- did I cool off in time` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 0 TRUE (`the calendar date` 13 11 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 307(6) -- did I cool off in time` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 0 TRUE (`the calendar date` 14 11 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307(6) -- did I cool off in time` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 0 TRUE (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 307(6) -- did I cool off in time` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 0 TRUE (`the calendar date` 5 11 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307(6) -- did I cool off in time` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 0 FALSE (`the calendar date` 10 11 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 307(6) -- did I cool off in time` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 1 TRUE (`the calendar date` 16 11 2026) EQUALS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 307(6) -- what can I be charged after cooling off` TRUE 1200 800 EQUALS JUST 1200
#ASSERT `s 307(6) -- what can I be charged after cooling off` FALSE 1200 800 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 308, 309 -- uplift fees and contingency fees`

#ASSERT `s 308(4) -- the largest uplift fee` TRUE 20000 EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 308(4) -- the largest uplift fee` FALSE 20000 EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 308 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5000 20000 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 308 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5000.01 20000 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 308 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 1000 20000 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 308 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 9000 20000 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 308 -- is my uplift fee allowed` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1000 20000 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 308 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1000 20000 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 308 -- is my uplift fee allowed` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 1000 20000 EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 309 -- is it a prohibited contingency fee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 309 -- is it a prohibited contingency fee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 309 -- is it a prohibited contingency fee` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 311 -- void agreements`

-- Arguments: written, by offer, offer states, excludes assessment, sophisticated, conditional, kind, success, plain,
-- signed, advice statement, cooling-off days, has uplift, uplift basis, uplift estimate, litigious, belief, uplift fee,
-- costs otherwise payable, share of recovery, only by scale.
-- A time-costing agreement, properly made.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 20000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT VOID`
-- A proper no-win no-fee agreement with a 25% uplift in litigation.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5000 20000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT VOID`
-- "30% of your payout".
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 20000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `VOID 309`
-- ... unless only by adopting a scale.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 20000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NOT VOID`
-- An uplift over 25% in litigation.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 6000 20000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VOID 308`
-- An uplift fee in an agreement that is not conditional.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1000 20000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VOID 308`
-- A conditional agreement with only 3 cooling-off days.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 20000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VOID 307`
-- A conditional agreement in a family law matter.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 20000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VOID 307`
-- Not written or evidenced in writing.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 20000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VOID 306`
-- Accepted by conduct, the offer not saying so.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 20000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VOID 306`
-- Contracting out of assessment: void for an individual, allowed for a sophisticated client.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 20000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VOID 306`
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 20000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT VOID`
-- Several faults: the most serious (s 309) is reported.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- is my costs agreement void` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `CLAIM` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 3 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 9000 20000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `VOID 309`

-- Repayments. s 309: everything paid.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `it charged a share of what I recovered (s 309)` 10000 2000 9000 10000 2000 EQUALS 12000
-- s 308: the uplift paid, and the rest above the lesser of 9,000 and 10,000.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `its uplift fee broke s 308` 10000 2000 9000 10000 2000 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `s 311 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `its uplift fee broke s 308` 10000 2000 12000 10000 2000 EQUALS 2000
-- Another contravention: paid 10,000; scale 8,000; agreement 9,000: repay 2,000.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `it broke another rule of Division 5 (s 306 or s 307)` 10000 0 8000 9000 0 EQUALS 2000
-- ... scale 11,000 but agreement 9,500: capped at the agreement, repay 500.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `it broke another rule of Division 5 (s 306 or s 307)` 10000 0 11000 9500 0 EQUALS 500
-- ... paid less than either: nothing to repay.
#ASSERT `s 311 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `it broke another rule of Division 5 (s 306 or s 307)` 5000 0 8000 9000 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 311 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `nothing: it is not void` 10000 2000 8000 9000 2000 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 312 -- setting aside`

#ASSERT `s 312 -- can I apply to set aside my costs agreement` `the client (the person the legal services are for)` FALSE EQUALS `yes: I may apply, and the costs assessor may set it aside if satisfied it is not fair or reasonable (s 312(1))`
#ASSERT `s 312 -- can I apply to set aside my costs agreement` `the client (the person the legal services are for)` TRUE EQUALS `yes: I may apply, and the costs assessor may set it aside if satisfied it is not fair or reasonable (s 312(1))`
#ASSERT `s 312 -- can I apply to set aside my costs agreement` `an associated third party payer who made the agreement, without the client being a party` FALSE EQUALS `yes: I may apply, and the costs assessor may set it aside if satisfied it is not fair or reasonable (s 312(1))`
-- s 300(3): a payer party alongside the client may apply only if it was not given a disclosure it was owed.
#ASSERT `s 312 -- can I apply to set aside my costs agreement` `an associated third party payer who made the agreement together with the client` TRUE EQUALS `yes: I may apply because the law practice did not make a disclosure owed to me (s 300(3)), and the costs assessor may set it aside if satisfied it is not fair or reasonable (s 312(1))`
#ASSERT `s 312 -- can I apply to set aside my costs agreement` `an associated third party payer who made the agreement together with the client` FALSE EQUALS `no: only the client, an associated third party payer party to the agreement without the client, or one not given a disclosure it was owed may apply (ss 300(3), 312(1), (12), 306(6))`
#ASSERT `s 312 -- can I apply to set aside my costs agreement` `someone else` TRUE EQUALS `no: only the client, an associated third party payer party to the agreement without the client, or one not given a disclosure it was owed may apply (ss 300(3), 312(1), (12), 306(6))`
#ASSERT `s 312 -- can I apply to set aside my costs agreement` `someone else` FALSE EQUALS `no: only the client, an associated third party payer party to the agreement without the client, or one not given a disclosure it was owed may apply (ss 300(3), 312(1), (12), 306(6))`

#ASSERT `s 312(6) -- the most I can be ordered to pay` 15000 12000 EQUALS 12000
#ASSERT `s 312(6) -- the most I can be ordered to pay` 9000 12000 EQUALS 9000

